    "submission_date": "2020-05-26",
    "abstract": "DETR views object detection as a direct set prediction problem, removing hand-designed components such as non-maximum suppression and anchor generation. A set-based global loss forces unique predictions via bipartite matching, and a transformer encoder-decoder reasons about object relations and global image context to output the final set of predictions in parallel from a fixed set of learned object queries. DETR matches a well-optimised Faster R-CNN on COCO.",
    "domain": "CV",
    "key_claims": [
      "Detection can be trained end-to-end as set prediction with a Hungarian-matching loss, without NMS or anchors.",
      "A transformer encoder-decoder with learned object queries predicts all objects in parallel.",
      "DETR R50 reaches 42.0 AP on COCO val, comparable to a tuned Faster R-CNN, with better large-object performance and worse small-object performance.",
      "Auxiliary decoding losses at every decoder layer help training.",
      "DETR extends to panoptic segmentation with a mask head."
    ],
    "parsed_at": "2026-10-23T12:00:00+05:30",
